      "comment": "SIR LUNCHALOTS (9) is the one to beat despite a plain recent form line, with his broader profile stronger than the last-start tenth at Moruya suggests. He has solid 1200m credentials, handles good ground and joins the Tanya Parry stable for his first Queensland run, which gives him a genuine reset. DANCE WIZZARD (3) brings the most obvious winning form after scoring at Cloncurry and has already shown he handles this track and distance, though he rises from BM55 company. A BAR IN PARIS (5) was third behind DANCE WIZZARD first-up and has the winning rider back, so she can tighten that margin if she improves second-up. RICALLEN (10) drops back from a Class 3 over 1400m, gets weight relief and had won a BM50 at Gladstone two back, leaving him as a sound place danger from a favourable setup.",
